## 4. Non-Negotiable Technical & Security Invariants
- `inputs/` is strictly **read-only**; intermediates go to `build/`, QA evidence to `preview/`, approved deliverables to `output/`.
- Secrets stay in `.env` (gitignored); `.env.example` documents keys only.
- `mtsk doctor` verifies environment readiness; deliverable acceptance requires domain evidence (`preview/`).
- Active security scans/DAST are strictly scoped to `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, or project-owned local Docker containers.

## 5. Red-Zone Boundaries (Explicit Human Authorization Required)
- Modifying or deleting source files in `inputs/` or custom user/team rules
- Destructive schema migrations (`DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, irreversible data loss)
- Installing external third-party MCP servers, global packages, or unvetted skills
- Production deployments, publishing (`npm publish`), paid API costs, or external data transfers

